I've left out the enrichment fetch. The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0`, and that clause is its entire authority. Importing `aap:caps/http-client@0.1.0` would put an interface in the world that the graph never granted, so the node would fail the capability check. Also, neither `Selection` nor `RunInfo` has a text field to put in `q=`.

To add the fetch properly, the platform team's approval needs to go into the graph first: add `HTTPClient<[metadata.internal.example]>` to `ComposeDigest`'s `with` clause and say which input field supplies `q`. After that, the body only needs `use crate::aap::caps::http_client::fetch;` and a call whose result is thrown away. The output stays the same either way, as you asked.

